PoolSyncJob in Runner service creates or re-image VM after workflow execution: {
  shape: sequence_diagram
  PoolSyncJob
  IMS

  PoolSyncJob.'Pool.Image -> ImageKey { source: "Curated", id: 1, version: "latest" }'
  PoolSyncJob -> IMS: "Get image reference by ImageKey"
  IMS."ImageKey: { source: 'Curated', id: 1, version: 'latest' }"
  IMS."ImageReference: {\nid:'/subscriptions/.../resourceGroups/.../providers/\nMicrosoft.Compute/galleries/.../images/.../versions/...',\noffer: ...,\npublisher: ... ,\nsku: ... ,\nversion: ...\n}"
  IMS -> PoolSyncJob: ImageReference
  PoolSyncJob -> PoolSyncJob: Create VM using ImageReference and\nprepare VM for workflow execution
  PoolSyncJob -> PoolSyncJob: Wait for workflow completion on VM

  PoolSyncJob -> IMS: "Get image reference by ImageKey\n{ source: 'Curated', id: 1, version: 'latest' }"
  PoolSyncJob."ImageReference response is cached in memory cache\non deployment level with 5 minutes expiration"
  PoolSyncJob."If request to IMS fails, Runner fallbacks to last known image reference"
  IMS -> PoolSyncJob: ImageReference
  PoolSyncJob -> PoolSyncJob: If image reference was changed, delete existing VM and create a new one.\nIf image reference is the same, re-image existing VM.

  PoolSyncJob -> PoolSyncJob: Wait for workflow completion on VM
  PoolSyncJob -> PoolSyncJob: "..."
}
